// Unchecked external call: a low-level call (`call`/`delegatecall`/
// `staticcall`-shaped) that reverted, while the enclosing transaction
// as a whole still completed with `status: success`.
//
// Why this pair of facts is the right structural signature: the EVM
// does not automatically propagate a `CALL`'s failure to its caller —
// a failed low-level call simply returns `false`; unless the caller
// explicitly checks that return value and reverts, execution
// continues and the transaction can still succeed overall. So a call
// that failed (`fact_model::Call::succeeded == false`) sitting inside
// a transaction that nonetheless reports `TxStatus::Success` is
// exactly what "the return value was never checked" looks like from
// the outside of a single-trace fact model — if the caller *had*
// checked it and reverted, the transaction's own status would be
// `Reverted`, not `Success` (see `demo/checked_call_reverts.json` for
// that contrasting shape).
//
// Both facts already existed in `fact-model` before this pattern
// (`Call::succeeded`, `Transaction`'s status) and both predicates
// already existed in the DSL/matcher (`call`, `transaction`) — the
// only change this pattern required was exposing the pre-existing
// `Call::succeeded` field as a `call(succeeded: ...)` filter attribute
// (`crates/dsl/src/schema.rs`, `crates/matcher/src/predicate.rs`),
// exactly the minimal extension the top-level README's exploit-corpus
// table proposed for this family.
//
// Scope note: this pattern flags "a call failed inside an otherwise-
// successful transaction" as a reviewable candidate. It cannot (and
// does not claim to) distinguish a genuinely unchecked low-level call
// from one whose failure was deliberately tolerated by design (e.g. a
// best-effort notification call the contract intentionally ignores) —
// the fact model has no "was this failure handled" flag, only whether
// the call itself succeeded. See the taxonomy crate's SCWE-048 /
// SWC-104 mapping notes for the same caveat in context.
pattern unchecked_external_call version 1 {
    family: UncheckedExternalCall
    severity: High
    tags: ["unchecked-call", "return-value", "error-handling"]
    references: ["SWC-104", "SCWE-048"]

    evidence {
        required failed_call: call(kind: External, succeeded: false)
        required tx_succeeded: transaction(status: Success)
    }

    constraint: AND(failed_call, tx_succeeded)
}
